            <div xml:id="d439">

                <pb facs="0507" n="491" sameAs="frus:frus1947v08/pg491"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">740.00119 Council/3–1147: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Ambassador in Brazil</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                        >Pawley</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of State </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">secret</hi>
                    </seg>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Rio de Janeiro</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1947-03-11T19:00:00-03:00">March 11, 1947—7
                            p.m.</date>
                    </dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>288. London’s telegram 1154, February 20. Embassy is not aware of any undertaking
                    “to make satisfactory arrangements with Brazil in the matter of reparations
                    outside the scope of the Paris Act”.</p>
                <p>This Embassy will be interested in learning if any conversations this regard were
                    carried on either Washington or London.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Pawley</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
